<title>USA: FSA qualifies eight muni issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies eight muni issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said on Wednesday it qualified for bond insurance the following eight municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Imperial Unified School District, Calif., $2 million general obligation (GO) bonds.</p>
<p>--Le Mars Community School District, Iowa, $2.205 million bonds.</p>
<p>--Ill., $60 million sales tax revenues.</p>
<p>--Mass., $200 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Woburn, Mass., $7.045 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Woodbury, Minn., $8.8 million GOs.</p>
<p>--East Aurora Unified School District, N.Y., $9.9 million.</p>
<p>--Huber Heights, Ohio, $2.045 million, street improvement.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
